            <title>[LU-21255] sanity-ec: MDS LBUG lu_device_fini() ASSERTION ld_ref == 0 in osp_device_free at MDT umount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21255</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/1ad8b17f-471d-49cf-947c-efc2ae4fabad" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/1ad8b17f-471d-49cf-947c-efc2ae4fabad&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.120&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137030" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137030&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.120&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137030" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/137030&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 6.12.0-211.68.1.el10_2_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity-ec suite crash at MDT unmount after the suite finished (review-dne-zfs-part-2, el10.2, ZFS, 4 MDTs):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LustreError: 716605:0:(lu_object.c:1054:lu_site_print()) header@...[0x12, 1, &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0x2000059f1:0x4:0x0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; hash exist]&lt;/p&gt;
{ mdt-object, mdd-object, lod-object, osp-object }
&lt;p&gt;LustreError: 716605:0:(lu_object.c:1292:lu_device_fini()) ASSERTION( atomic_read(&amp;amp;d-&amp;gt;ld_ref) == 0 ) failed: Refcount is 1&lt;br/&gt;
LustreError: 716605:0:(lu_object.c:1292:lu_device_fini()) LBUG&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stack (umount): lu_device_fini &amp;lt;- osp_device_free &amp;lt;- obd_cleanup &amp;lt;- class_free_dev &amp;lt;- class_detach &amp;lt;- class_manual_cleanup &amp;lt;- osp_obd_disconnect &amp;lt;- lod_putref &amp;lt;- lod_fini_tgt &amp;lt;- lod_device_fini &amp;lt;- class_cleanup. Node: MDS (MDT0001 stop, "umount -d -f /mnt/lustre-mds2"), right after "sanity-ec test complete" and "finish cleanup"; sanity-ec test_310 skipped (FIEMAP on ZFS). An earlier lfsck_namespace osd_index_it_key field-spanning-write WARNING is in the same dmesg (sanity-lfsck, earlier in the session).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A remote MDT object (mdt/mdd/lod/osp stack) still holds a reference on the osp device when the MDT is stopped. The same assertion text appears client side in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20509" title="sanity-sec test_54: lu_object.c:1297:lu_device_fini() ASSERTION( atomic_read(&amp;amp;d-&amp;gt;ld_ref) == 0 ) " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20509"&gt;LU-20509&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12571" title="sanity-dom test_150: ASSERTION( atomic_read(&amp;amp;d-&amp;gt;ld_ref) == 0 ) failed: Refcount is 1" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12571"&gt;LU-12571&lt;/a&gt; (lovsub_device_free), a different device stack, so this server side osp variant is not covered by them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The change under test (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21025" title="quota: slave doesn't reintegrate after LWP reconnects to restarted master" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21025"&gt;LU-21025&lt;/a&gt; quota qsd reintegration) touches only lustre/quota/qsd_*.c and takes no lu_object references, so the crash is not caused by it. Rainshadow counts 38 branch and 22 other change failures with this assertion text in 30 days (mostly sanity-sec test_54, client side).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/1ad8b17f-471d-49cf-947c-efc2ae4fabad" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/1ad8b17f-471d-49cf-947c-efc2ae4fabad&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69999-ps6-63a8029c2a6e on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69999" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69999&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
